{
  "name": "bone_crab",
  "version": 1,
  "introduced_by": "ribshore",
  "notes": "wade: A crab far larger than any living one, near three metres across the legs: a deep rust shell studded with pale knobs over slate-blue legs, one great crushing claw. Scuttles sideways over the shore and the shallows, picking at whatever the tide leaves, and settles flat on the sand to rest. Walks to its right: the model is drawn with that side at -Z.",
